19\tSubjects, not authorities: `generated/hello-world.mjs`,\n    20\t`test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs` and `test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs` were\n    21\tsupplied without accepted behavior or author provenance. They are evaluated\n    22\tagainst this document. They do not define its meaning. Neither the test names, a\n    23\tpredecessor's CLI behavior nor current code may reinterpret any requirement below.\n    24\t\n    25\t## 2. Intent\n    26\t\n    27\tBuild a minimal Node.js command-line \"Hello World\" program by a complete,\n    28\ttraceable software-build traversal: conformance, implementation design, source,\n    29\ttest design, component test source, UAT test source, test execution plan and\n    30\ttest execution result. The observable Product outcome is simple: a user runs\n    31\tthe CLI with Node, with no install step, and sees exactly `Hello, world!`\n    32\tfollowed by one newline, and the process exits successfully. Real execution of\n    33\tthe CLI and of both tests must prove this. A written claim does not.\n    34\t\n    35\t## 3. Product boundary\n    36\t\n    37\t**Inside the Product**\n    38\t\n    39\t- One application source surface: `generated/hello-world.mjs`, an ES module run\n    40\t  directly by `node`.\n    41\t- One supported public entry: `node generated/hello-world.mjs`, run from the\n    42\t  project root with no arguments.\n    43\t- Public exits: the bytes written to stdout and the process exit status.\n    44\t\n    45\t**Inside the traversal but not the runtime Product.** These are the verification\n    46\tand lifecycle assets that realize the original stage meanings:\n    47\t`specification/project-conformance.md`, `design/implementation-design.md`,\n    48\t`design/test-design.md`, `test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs`,\n    49\t`test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs`, `test-execution-plan.json` and the admitted\n    50\tcommand-execution evidence that carries the `test_execution_result` meaning.\n    51\t\n    52\t**Outside the Product**\n    53\t\n    54\t- Command-line arguments, flags, help or version output, stdin, environment-driven\n    55\t  behavior and localization.\n    56\t- Any `package.json`, lockfile, `node_modules`, npm scripts, build or transpile\n    57\t  step, `bin` installation, publishing, or network access.\n    58\t- Runtimes other than Node.\n    59\t- The GTL/HoG/ABG library, `.ai-workspace/` and all installed assets. These are\n    60\t  the Development Product that carries out the traversal. They are not the Hello\n    61\t  World Product and must not be confused with it or changed by it.\n    62\t\n    63\t## 4. Traversal declaration\n    64\t\n    65\t| Stage (original) | Artifact | Realization in this witness run |\n    66\t|---|---|---|\n    67\t| `conformance_project` | `specification/project-conformance.md` | Newly authored (this file). |\n    68\t| `implementation_design` | `design/implementation-design.md` | Must be newly authored. This file is its authority. |\n    69\t| `source` | `generated/hello-world.mjs` | Supplied CLI. A baseline measurement came first, then a bounded correction (see §7). |\n    70\t| `test_design` | `design/test-design.md` | Must be newly authored. |\n    71\t| `component_test_source` | `test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs` | Supplied verifier, protected. It is reused only if it meets AC-05. It is not counted as newly authored work. |\n    72\t| `uat_test_source` | `test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs` | Supplied verifier, protected. It is reused only if it meets AC-06. It is not counted as newly authored work. |\n    73\t| `test_execution_plan` | `test-execution-plan.json` | Must be newly authored. It is a prospective declaration only (see C2 and C3). |\n    74\t| `test_execution_result` | none (the original says \"Produce no files\") | Admitted C2 command-execution observations, judged under AC-12 by an independent assessment. |\n    75\t\n    76\t## 5. Requirements\n    77\t\n    78\tEach requirement cites its source as *file › stage › instruction*.\n    79\t\"Project root\" means the worksite root that contains `generated/`, `test/` and\n    80\t`source/`.\n    81\t\n    82\t- **REQ-01 Source surface.** The application source surface is exactly\n    83\t  `generated/hello-world.mjs`.\n    84\t  *Original › conformance_project: \"The source surface must be\n    85\t  generated/hello-world.mjs.\"; implementation_design: \"Define a minimal Node CLI\n    86\t  script at generated/hello-world.mjs.\"; oracle › requiredArtifacts.*\n    87\t- **REQ-02 No installation.** The script runs under `node` with no package\n    88\t  installation, no dependency outside `node:` built-ins, and no network access.\n    89\t  *Original › source: \"The script must execute under node without package\n    90\t  installation.\"; contract: \"There is no package/network dependency for this\n    91\t  application.\"*\n    92\t- **REQ-03 Exact stdout.** Running `node generated/hello-world.mjs` from the\n    93\t  project root with no arguments writes exactly `\"Hello, world!\\n\"` to stdout:\n    94\t  capital `H`, a comma after `Hello`, one space, lowercase `world`, `!`, then\n    95\t  exactly one LF. Nothing else is written: no leading or trailing whitespace, no\n    96\t  BOM, no CR and no further lines.\n    97\t  *Original › conformance_project, implementation_design and source; oracle ›\n    98\t  cases[0].stdout.*\n    99\t- **REQ-04 Successful exit.** The same run terminates normally with exit status\n   100\t  `0`.\n   101\t  *Original › test_design and component_test_source: \"assert status 0\"; oracle ›\n   102\t  cases[0].exitStatus; contract: \"exits zero\".*\n   103\t- **REQ-05 Execution proof.** The proof must actually run the CLI and observe\n   104\t  its stdout. Inspecting the source text does not prove REQ-03 or REQ-04.\n   105\t  *Original › conformance_project: \"The execution proof must run the CLI and\n   106\t  observe stdout exactly\"; contract: \"Both supplied tests must actually execute\n   107\t  the current CLI.\"*\n   108\t- **REQ-06 Component verifier.** `test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs` uses\n   109\t  `node:test`, `node:assert/strict` and `spawnSync` from `node:child_process`. It\n   110\t  runs `process.execPath` with `[\"generated/hello-world.mjs\"]` from the project\n   111\t  root and asserts status `0` and stdout exactly `\"Hello, world!\\n\"`.\n   112\t  *Original › component_test_source.*\n   113\t- **REQ-07 UAT verifier.** `test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs` uses the same\n   114\t  modules and spawn mechanism and asserts that the user-visible CLI output is\n   115\t  exactly `\"Hello, world!\\n\"`. Under REQ-09 it also asserts status `0`.\n   116\t  *Original › uat_test_source; test_design.*\n   117\t- **REQ-08 Implementation design.** `design/implementation-design.md` takes this\n   118\t  conformance asset as its authority. It defines the minimal Node CLI script at\n   119\t  `generated/hello-world.mjs` that prints exactly `Hello, world!` followed by one\n   120\t  newline. It names the component and UAT test source surfaces that execute the\n   121\t  CLI and assert stdout.\n   122\t  *Original › implementation_design; contract: \"realizable design faithful to the\n   123\t  original outcome and the conformance asset, including source and verification\n   124\t  surfaces\".*\n   125\t- **REQ-09 Test design.** `design/test-design.md` specifies component and UAT\n   126\t  validation of the CLI stdout contract. Both tests spawn\n   127\t  `node generated/hello-world.mjs` and assert status `0` and stdout exactly\n   128\t  `\"Hello, world!\\n\"`.\n   129\t  *Original › test_design; contract: \"meaningful component and user-outcome checks\n   130\t  of the actual CLI\".*\n   131\t- **REQ-10 Execution plan.** `test-execution-plan.json` declares:\n   132\t  - `command` `\"node\"` and `args`\n   133\t    `[\"--test\", \"test/component/hello-cli.test.mjs\", \"test/uat/hello-cli.uat.test.mjs\"]`;\n   134\t  - `expectedTestPassCount` ≥ 2