{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWheFCCamgnk3PzApUky","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q8rahtVqJ1Dtjn9hD7FVbL","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"summary":"I wrote the three assets in my write scope. All three were absent before this vector, and I wrote nothing else. None of them accepts anything.\n\n1. **`design/implementation-design.md`** (sha256 801f3ab5…)\n   - **Authority:** cites `specification/project-conformance.md` (a74a75b6…), with the original source, contract and oracle ranked above it.\n   - **Design decision:** one dependency-free ES module at `generated/hello-world.mjs`. Its exact 30-byte content is `console.log(\"Hello, world!\");` plus a newline, given as hex. It explains step by step why this gives exactly the 14 stdout bytes 48656c6c6f2c20776f726c64210a and exits 0:\n     - with one argument and no `%`, `util.format` returns the literal unchanged;\n     - Node's console always appends LF, never `os.EOL`, so no CR is written;\n     - the literal is ASCII and no BOM is written;\n     - with no `process.exit` or `exitCode`, the process exits 0 naturally.\n   - **Alternatives:** `process.stdout.write` with the newline is permitted but not selected. Ruled out: `process.exit`, a missing or doubled newline, computed greetings, package, bin or build steps, and any extra output.\n   - **Boundaries:** the public entry and exits, and a failure-mode table.\n   - **Verification surfaces:** both protected tests (by digest and test name) and both fixed commands. It also covers the cwd, interpreter and currentness seams.\n   - **Correspondence:** a table mapping the design to AC-09.\n   - **Lineage:** the baseline failure on 647697a5… was a wrong literal, not a wrong mechanism. The correction produced fe8f4080…. The current bytes match the design, so no further CLI change is needed, and the baseline stays historical.\n   - **Frame families:** proposes Design Component and Insta